<title>NETHERLANDS: Bangert-Pontier cuts Endemol to a Sell.</title>
<headline>Bangert-Pontier cuts Endemol to a Sell.</headline>
<dateline>AMSTERDAM 1997-04-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Summary of April research.</p>
<p>Company------Sector-----------Price-----Broker--------------</p>
<p>Endemol	TV production    58.10     Bank Bangert-Pontier</p>
<p>COMMENT: Sell (vs Hold)</p>
<p>Results for first half of 1996/97 disappointing, operating margins down to 11.1 pct from 13.6 pct. Share of live entertainment division, where margins are traditionally lower, on total group sales rose to 25 percent from 13 percent.</p>
<p>Although we see growth potential for Endemol, we consider the shares overvalued at the current full-year 1996/97 price-earnings multiple of over 26.  </p>
<p>    Estimates (NLG):  EPS     pvs EPS   P/E    Dividend</p>
<p>    1996/97	     2.20    (2.40)    26.4   0.60</p>
<p>    1997/98	     2.45    (2.65)    23.7   0.70</p>
<p>    1998/99	     2.70    (2.90)    21.4   0.80</p>
<p>-- Amsterdam newsroom, +31 20 504 5000 (Fax +31 20 504 5040)</p>
